      "dom_id": "question-67482",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that a geometric sequence has the $4$th term ${a}_{4}=250$ and the common ratio $r=5$, what is the index of the term $1\\,250?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we are given that ${a}_{4}=250$, we can use the formula for the $n$th term to solve for ${a}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{4-1} \\\\ 250 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4-1} \\\\ 250 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{250}{125} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n}=2\\cdot {5}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=1\\,250,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,250 & =2\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{1\\,250}{2} & ={5}^{n-1} \\\\ 625 & ={5}^{n-1} \\\\ {5}^{4} & ={5}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n4=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=5\n$$",
